\details{
Several steps of the original silently drop records, and the SQL reproduces
them on purpose, since the aim is the same records rather than tidier ones: a
numeric measurement with no mapped unit disappears, a missing
\code{measurement_datetime} is not filled from \code{measurement_date}, and a drug
exposure with no end date is dropped. The SQL files name each case, and the
project's \code{OPEN_QUESTIONS.md} records how each was confirmed against
pandas.

The measurement side is deliberately aligned to FeatureExtraction so that a
\code{featureExtractionLong.csv} row can be turned back into an \code{allrecords}
token by \code{\link[=covariateToToken]{covariateToToken()}}: the concept filter is \verb{concept_id <> 0} and
nothing else, the value comes from \code{value_as_number}, and the unit is grouped
by \code{unit_concept_id}. The SQL files say where each decision comes from.

The measurement quantiles are not applied here: \code{\link[=createAllRecords]{createAllRecords()}} applies
them at the end, once the quantile table exists.
